      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.08,
          "end": 5.76,
          "en": "We're using v-for with an array like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.76,
          "end": 8.91,
          "en": "And that is honestly also probably",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.91,
          "end": 11.13,
          "en": "the most common way of using it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.13,
          "end": 14.71,
          "en": "But v-for has a couple of interesting variations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.71,
          "end": 16.97,
          "en": "For one, you can, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.97,
          "end": 19.81,
          "en": "pull out more than just the array item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.81,
          "end": 23.4,
          "en": "You can also get the index off the item in the array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.4,
          "end": 27.51,
          "en": "And doing so is simple, you just wrap your item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.51,
          "end": 29.4,
          "en": "which you're pulling out off the array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.4,
          "end": 32.513,
          "en": "with every iteration between parentheses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.96,
          "end": 35.72,
          "en": "and then add a comma.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.72,
          "end": 38.37,
          "en": "And now you can add a second item here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.37,
          "end": 39.48,
          "en": "give it any name you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.48,
          "end": 43.69,
          "en": "like index or idx and going forward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.69,
          "end": 47.14,
          "en": "Index here, and this will be the index off this item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.14,
          "end": 49.94,
          "en": "So that's another syntex supported by Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.94,
          "end": 51.8,
          "en": "getting not just the item itself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.8,
          "end": 54.583,
          "en": "but also its index with this notation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.36,
          "end": 59.27,
          "en": "And now here we could, for example, add a dash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.27,
          "end": 62.83,
          "en": "and that's not special Vue syntex, that's just a dash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.83,
          "end": 67.48,
          "en": "And then again add interpolation to all the output index,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.48,
          "end": 68.483,
          "en": "if we want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.52,
          "end": 71.37,
          "en": "I'll quickly reformat that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.37,
          "end": 73.84,
          "en": "And if I saved it and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.84,
          "end": 77.35,
          "en": "if I start adding goals, you see here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.35,
          "end": 79.51,
          "en": "this has the index zero because it was",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.51,
          "end": 84.51,
          "en": "the first goal I added, master Vue has index one and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.53,
          "end": 86.66,
          "en": "So that can also be useful in cases",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.66,
          "end": 88.223,
          "en": "where you need the index.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.31,
          "end": 94.25999999999999,
          "en": "Now you can also loop through more than just arrays.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.25999999999999,
          "end": 97.45,
          "en": "You can also loop through objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.45,
          "end": 102.17,
